{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/ClusteringCoefficients","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/CoreNumbers","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques"],"title":"Structures","generated":true},{"title":"Extended Modules","anchor":"Extended-Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols"],"generated":true}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module","externalID":"Cliques","modules":[{"name":"Cliques"}],"role":"collection","title":"Cliques"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/cliques"]}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols","role":"collection","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols","title":"GraphProtocols"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/ClusteringCoefficients":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/ClusteringCoefficients","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ClusteringCoefficients"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Triangles and clustering for every vertex of an undirected graph’s simple graph, from one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pass (JGraphT’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ClusteringCoefficient"},{"type":"text","text":"; NetworkX "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"triangles"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clustering"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transitivity"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"average_clustering"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"title":"ClusteringCoefficients","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/clusteringcoefficients","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ClusteringCoefficients"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/CoreNumbers":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The core decomposition of an undirected graph (Batagelj–Zaversnik; NetworkX "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"core_number"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"igraph "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreness"},{"type":"text","text":", JGraphT "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Coreness"},{"type":"text","text":"), over its simple graph: a vertex’s core number"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is the largest k such that it lies in a subgraph where every vertex has at least k neighbors."}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/corenumbers","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CoreNumbers","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/CoreNumbers","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CoreNumbers","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"CoreNumbers"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"type":"topic","title":"Cliques","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","abstract":[],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques":{"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MaximalCliques"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MaximalCliques"}],"title":"MaximalCliques"}}}